id: pm-w7clh6
title: update-many silently drops a null update field in the flat transport instead of clearing it or refusing
description: "Found by Codex review of the GH-1655 change (pm-gh1655). updateManyOptionsFromFlat in src/sdk/runtime-input.ts normalizes a flat update field whose value is null to undefined, so runAction('update-many', { ids: [id], assignee: null, description: 'changed' }) changes the description and silently keeps the assignee. The nested form ({ update: { assignee: null } }) reaches resolveUpdateTransportOptions and is folded into unset by pm-gh1655, so the two spellings of one request disagree. The flat form mixes selection filters and update fields in one record, which is why pm-gh1655 kept update-many out of the null-clear contract (PmUpdateManyActionOptions stays non-nullable)."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: bulk,pm-gh1655,sdk,update-many
created_at: "2026-11-03T23:06:21.402Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T06:30:09.251Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A flat update-many payload with a null on a clearable update field (one the update unset table covers) clears it exactly like the nested form ({ update: { field: null } }); it never silently drops it; A flat null on a non-clearable update field (for example title) refuses naming the field, exactly as the nested form and a single update refuse it; Flat and nested update-many spellings of the same request produce the same rows, clears and refusals alike, with a spec for each; A flat null on a key that is a selection filter rather than an update field is refused naming the key, never applied as a clear"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
expected_result: "A null on a clearable update field in a flat update-many payload clears it exactly like the nested form, and a null on a non-clearable field refuses like the nested form"
actual_result: The flat payload drops the null field silently while the rest of the update applies
